        "context": "[Ecdf00123e1bf105831e21391] [Bugfix] SharedStorage Connector for V1 PD multimodal > Purpose\nIt brings in the mm_hashes from the Request to the connector to form a proper key; that can help distinguish kv for different mm input. It fix the problems about wrongly reusing the kv mentioned in the issue.\nSupport multiple multimodal inputs as well.\n\n[Eb6bd4880e6f4528f68970222] [Bug]: Wrongly reuse KV, for V1 PD disaggregation with multimodal input > **Request 4 with Image C, after emptying shared_storage_path (Abnormal):**\n**This is likely due to the fact that, the key for KV transfer only depends on prompt_token_ids; Where number of placeholder tokens in it would be the same for different images with the same image size. I think this issue happen not only in SharedStorageConnector, but in V1 PD disagg in general? Since I didn't find any design specifically for multimodal V1 PD disagg?**\n\n[E66963e616c94bfb4a30bf988] Disaggregated Prefilling (experimental) > Development\n- **Connector**: Connector allows **kv consumer** to retrieve the KV caches of a batch of request from **kv producer**.\n- **LookupBuffer**: LookupBuffer provides two API: `insert` KV cache and `drop_select` KV cache.\nThe semantics of `insert` and `drop_select` are similar to SQL, where `insert` inserts a KV cache into the buffer, and `drop_select` returns the KV cache that matches the given condition and drop it from the buffer.\n\n[E6af440ee9c68dee53b325337] Troubleshooting and Frequently Asked Questions > Frequently Asked Questions > The results are not deterministic, even with a temperature of 0\nThis difference accumulates across many layers, resulting in nondeterministic output when the batch size changes.\nSimilarly, when prefix caching is enabled, it can also dispatch to different kernels.\nEven when the computations are mathematically equivalent, small numerical differences from different kernel implementations lead to the final nondeterministic outputs.\n\n[E4687c385ca9ba1960be54be6] Disaggregated Prefilling (experimental) > Third-party contributions\n- **Fully-customized connector**: Implement your own `Connector`, and call third-party libraries to send and receive KV caches, and many many more (like editing vLLM's model input to perform customized prefilling, etc).\nThis approach gives you the most control, but at the risk of being incompatible with future vLLM versions.\n\n[E3a24be83b77ea79afd19892a] [Bug]: Wrongly reuse KV, for V1 PD disaggregation with multimodal input > 🐛 Describe the bug\nI tried these requests in a single instance (PD mix) case, and a 1P1D disaggregation case in V1.\nThe outputs in PD disagg are similar/identical to the outputs from PD mix; Prefiller encode the mm_input, then prefill, then Decoder can successfully load KV stored from Prefiller and give decent results. I think we can assume that V1 PD disagg with mm input works fine in general, _except for below bug situation:\n\n[E297bcc5cca3d310f7d1263b0] Disaggregated Prefilling (experimental) > Usage example\n- **MultiConnector**: take advantage of the kv_connector_extra_config: dict[str, Any] already present in KVTransferConfig to stash all the connectors we want in an ordered list of kwargs.such as:",
